  "query_preview": "..This morning's patchy fog over southern Cochise \nand Santa Cruz Counties has dissipated with just some low-level \ncumulus left over. Arizona will be in between weather systems \ntoday and Thursday with dry westerly flow aloft. This will lead \nto dry conditions both days with high temperatures around \nnormal today and a few degrees above normal Thursday. \n\nFriday into Saturday a trough passes through central to northern\nArizona with some uncertainty still present in how far south it\nwill end up. As the trough moves through southeast Arizona will\nbe mostly dry with just a slight chance of precip in the White\nMountains Friday afternoon. Winds may also be a little breezy\nsouth of Tucson and in the White Mountains Friday. Ensembles \nthen bring another trough through the region early next week. \nHowever there are considerable differences between ensemble \nmodels in the strength of the low with the GEFS showing a \nstronger trough the the Euro, which shows a weak open wave. \nBecause of this NBM PoPs are greatly reduced in coverage \ncompared to 24 hours ago with just a slight chance for precip in\nthe White Mountains Monday. Temperatures this weekend into \nearly next week will be around normal to a few degrees below \nnormal.",
